From: Vadik Likholetov <vadikas@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 23:59:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: tegra-pkvm: trust firmware for walk coherency

The generic Arm SMMU driver treats firmware as authoritative for page-table
walk coherency even when IDR0.CTTW claims otherwise, since implementations
can expose an incorrectly configured ID bit.

Apply the same policy to the Tegra pKVM frontend. Tegra234 does not mark
these SMMU nodes dma-coherent, so the hypervisor must clean page-table
updates to PoC before the SMMU walks them. Skipping those cleans makes the
SMMU consume stale descriptors and corrupts host DMA.

---
 drivers/iommu/arm-smmu-tegra-pkvm.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm-smmu-tegra-pkvm.c b/drivers/iommu/arm-smmu-tegra-pkvm.c
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm-smmu-tegra-pkvm.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm-smmu-tegra-pkvm.c
@@ -391,7 +391,13 @@ static int pkvm_tegra_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	hyp_smmu->ias = pkvm_tegra_id_size(FIELD_GET(PKVM_SMMU_ID2_IAS, id2));
 	hyp_smmu->oas = pkvm_tegra_id_size(FIELD_GET(PKVM_SMMU_ID2_OAS, id2));
-	hyp_smmu->coherent_walk = of_dma_is_coherent(dev->of_node) ||
-				  !!(id0 & PKVM_SMMU_ID0_CTTW);
+	/*
+	 * Match the Arm SMMU driver's coherency policy: firmware is the
+	 * authority even when IDR0.CTTW advertises coherent table walks. This
+	 * also covers implementations whose ID register is configured
+	 * incorrectly. Tegra234 does not mark these SMMUs dma-coherent, so the
+	 * hypervisor must publish page-table updates explicitly.
+	 */
+	hyp_smmu->coherent_walk = of_dma_is_coherent(dev->of_node);
 	hyp_smmu->vmid16 = !!(id2 & PKVM_SMMU_ID2_VMID16);
 	if ((hyp_smmu->pgshift != 12 && hyp_smmu->pgshift != 16) ||
 	    hyp_smmu->mmio_size <
